        "original_id": "b9950d4a-dc84-50bb-a34c-3739c2442b95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David T. Beito, T. R. M. Howard, Medgar Evers, Fannie Lou Hamer\n- Organizations: Regional Council of Negro Leadership\n- Publications: The Wall Street Journal, Harper's Magazine\n- Topics: civil rights, self-help, business ownership, biography\n\nFacts:\n- Theodore Roosevelt Mason \"T. R. M.\" Howard was born on March 4, 1908, and died on May 1, 1976.\n- T. R. M. Howard was an American civil rights leader, fraternal organization leader, entrepreneur, and surgeon.\n- T. R. M. Howard founded the Regional Council of Negro Leadership in Mississippi in 1951.\n- The Regional Council of Negro Leadership promoted civil rights, self-help, and business ownership.\n- \"Black Maverick\" is a biography by David T. Beito about T. R. M. Howard.\n- T. R. M. Howard mentored Medgar Evers and Fannie Lou Hamer.\n- The Wall Street Journal and Harper's Magazine reviewed \"Black Maverick.\"",
